This extension adds FINAL FANTASY TACTICS - The Ivalice Chronicles modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Reloaded-II and FFTIVC ModLoader installed automatically.[/summary]

Steam version supported.
[b][size=3]This extension will automatically install [url=https://github.com/Reloaded-Project/Reloaded-II]Reloaded-II Mod Manager[/url] and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/finalfantasytacticstheivalicechronicles/mods/4]FFTIVC Mod Loader[/url].[/size][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][b][color=#ea9999]This game does not support symlinks. You must have the mod staging folder and the game on the same drive to use this extension.[/color][/b][/size]

[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Reloaded-II Mod Manager installs to the game folder, recognised by a "reloaded-ii.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Mod Loader installs to the "Reloaded\Mods\FFTIVC_Mod_Loader" folder, recognised by a "modconfig.json" file and a "fftivc.utility.modloader.dll" file.[/*]
[*]Reloaded mods with a "modconfig.json" file install to the "Reloaded\Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the game folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Reloaded-II Mod Manager will be automatically downloaded and installed into a "Reloaded" folder inside the game folder.[/*]
[*]The FFTIVC Mod Loader will be automatically installed to "Reloaded&#92;Mods&#92;FFTIVC_Mod_Loader" folder.[/*]
[*]Mods for Reloaded (have a "ModConfig.json" file) will be installed in the correct "Reloaded&#92;Mods" folder for the tool to load them.[/*]
[*][size=3][b][color=#ffff00]IMPORTANT: You may need to launch Reloaded-II as Administrator to allow it to download dependencies required by the game. This is only necessary if the game is installed in a privileged folder, such as [color=#ffff00]"C:&#92;Program Files (x86)"[/color]. This is the default install location for Steam on the C Drive. [/color][/b][/size][/*]
[*]Users will receive a notification after deploying mods with a button to run Reloaded as Admin.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for FINAL FANTASY TACTICS - The Ivalice Chronicles mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Reloaded-II (mod loader):

This installer handles Reloaded-II, not mods for it. It exists so users can install Reloaded-II through Vortex, and mod authors normally never package this.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a file named "reloaded-ii.exe" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If you bundle Reloaded-II inside your mod archive, Vortex treats the whole download as Reloaded-II rather than as your mod. Ship the mod alone and list Reloaded-II as a requirement.

========================================================================

Reloadedmodloader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "modconfig.json" file and a "fftivc.utility.modloader.dll" file.

  Installs to: "Reloaded\Mods\FFTIVC_Mod_Loader"

========================================================================

Reloadedmod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "modconfig.json" file.

  Installs to: "Reloaded\Mods"

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

The catch-all. Any archive that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied across unchanged.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report the mod as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine.
[/spoiler]

